      "So-called dumb money really did make mistake as retail appears to have bought Oracle ahead of earnings",
      "JPMorgan's retail radar report, which attempts to strip out retail from institutional trading activity, noted individual investors poured into Oracle ahead of the company's fiscal fourth-quarter results.",
      "That certainly hasn't worked out with stock down by a double-digit percentage into the open. But retail investors were net sellers of tech through the week to June 10, the JPMorgan report found."
